message.content:
I found two likely periapical lesions, both in the lower jaw on the patient's right. Both look faint, so treat the grades as tentative. I graded them by eye from enlarged, contrast-boosted crops, without a clinical exam or other X-rays.

```json
{"lesions": [
  {"box": [0.394, 0.679, 0.423, 0.743], "pai": 3},
  {"box": [0.269, 0.623, 0.297, 0.675], "pai": 3}
]}
```

1. **Root fragment near the lower right canine:** a poorly defined dark area surrounds a leftover root. The bone there looks changed and partly demineralised, but the area has no clear border, so it rates a 3 rather than a 4.
2. **Lower right molar roots:** there is a slight dark area between the root tips. It could be a small early lesion or a loss of bone between the roots from gum disease. I scored it 3, but it is the less certain of the two.

I also looked at the decayed lower left molar. The bone around its root tips looked normal to slightly changed, so I left it out.
